 of Ca<sup>2+</sup>-activated Cl<sup>- </sup>channels in <italic>Xenopus </italic>oocytes</article-title><source>Pflugers Arch</source><year>1992</year><volume>420</volume><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>229</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1320252</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF00374996</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dascal</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Gillo</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Lass</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of calcium mobilization in mediation of acetylcholine-evoked chloride currents in <italic>Xenopus laevis </italic>oocytes</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><year>1985</year><volume>366</volume><fpage>299</fpage><lpage>313</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2414433</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Miledi</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A calcium-dependent transient outward current in <italic>Xenopus laevis </italic>oocytes</article-title><source>Proc R Soc Lond B Biol Sci</source><year>1982</year><volume>215</volume><fpage>491</fpage><lpage>497</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6127718</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barish</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A transient calcium-dependent chloride current in the immature <italic>Xenopus </italic>oocytes</article-title><source>J Physiol</source><year>1983</year><volume>342</volume><fpage>309</fpage><lpage>325</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6313909</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dascal</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Snutch</surname><given-names>TP</given-names></name><name><surname>L&#x000fc;bbert</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Davidson</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Lester</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Expression and modulation of voltage-gated calcium channels after RNA injection in <italic>Xenopus </italic>oocytes</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1986</year><volume>231</volume><fpage>1147</fpage><lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2418503</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.2418503</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boton</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Gillo</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Dascal</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Lass</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Two calcium-activated chloride conductance in <italic>Xenopus laevis </italic>oocytes permeabilized with the ionophore A23187</article-title><source>J Physiol (Lond)</source><year>1989</year><volume>408</volume><fpage>511</fpage><lpage>534</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2506341</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boton</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Dascal</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inactivation of calcium-activated chloride conductance in <italic>Xenopus </italic>oocytes: roles of calcium and protein kinase C</article-title><source>Pflugers Arch</source><year>1990</year><volume>416</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1693766</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/BF00370214</